---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Size & Care Guide — AASRA" description="How to measure for curtains, choose rug sizes, and plan table settings.">
  <div class="page-title-block">
    <div class="kicker">Guides</div>
    <h1>Size &amp; care guide</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">Measure twice, order once — everything you need to choose the right size.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">
      <!-- Curtains -->
      <div class="guide-block reveal">
        <h2>Curtain panels</h2>
        <p>Our panels hang best with generous fullness — the fabric should gather, not stretch flat.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Width:</strong> measure the curtain rod from end to end, then add <strong>15–25 cm on each side</strong> so panels can stack clear of the glass. For soft gathering, order combined panel width equal to <strong>2× the rod length</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Drop (length):</strong> measure from the bottom of the rod ring to where you want the panel to end — <em>sill</em> (clean, practical), <em>below sill</em> (relaxed), or <em>floor</em> (formal). For a floor-length puddle, add 20–30 cm.</li>
          <li><strong>Example:</strong> a 2 m rod, floor-length hang → two 135 cm panels give beautiful fullness.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="guide-note">Our panels come in 135 × 240 cm and 135 × 270 cm. Unsure? Message us your window measurements on Email and we will tell you exactly what to order.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Rugs -->
      <div class="guide-block reveal">
        <h2>Rugs</h2>
        <p>The right rug grounds the room; the wrong size shrinks it. When in doubt, go bigger.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Living room:</strong> at minimum, the <strong>front legs of all main seating</strong> should rest on the rug. Our 4 × 6 ft suits compact lounges; a 6 × 9 ft anchors a full seating group.</li>
          <li><strong>Dining room:</strong> the rug should extend <strong>at least 60 cm beyond the table on all sides</strong>, so chairs stay on the rug even when pulled back.</li>
          <li><strong>Bedroom:</strong> a runner at the bedside, or a rug wide enough to step onto on both sides of the bed.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="guide-note">Flat-weave dhurries sit low, so they slide cleanly under doors and furniture where thicker rugs cannot.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Table -->
      <div class="guide-block reveal">
        <h2>Tableware</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Dinner plates (26 cm):</strong> the standard dinner size; allow <strong>60 cm of table width per place setting</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Serving bowl (28 cm):</strong> sized for a table of four to six; pair with the plate set for a complete setting.</li>
          <li><strong>Teak tray (45 × 30 cm):</strong> fits a standard coffee table with room for a cup beside it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="guide-note">All ceramics are dishwasher and microwave safe. Teak should be hand-wiped and oiled twice a year.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Care -->
      <div class="guide-block reveal">
        <h2>Care, in brief</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Linen:</strong> wash cool (30°C), mild detergent, line-dry in shade. The crease is the point — see the <a href="/journal/caring-for-linen" style="text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px;">linen care journal</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Dhurries:</strong> vacuum without a beater bar; blot spills cold; reversible, so rotate end-for-end monthly.</li>
          <li><strong>Stoneware:</strong> dishwasher safe; avoid thermal shock (no freezer-to-oven).</li>
          <li><strong>Teak:</strong> wipe dry after washing; food-safe oil twice a year.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="guide-note">Full care notes ship printed with every order.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="service-links" style="justify-content:center; margin-top:3rem;">
        <a href="mailto:orders@aasra.shop" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ask us on Email</a>
        <a href="/faq">Read the FAQ</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .guide-block { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 2.4rem 0; }
  .guide-block h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .guide-block > p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.85; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .guide-block ul { list-style: none; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .guide-block li { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.9; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; position: relative; }
  .guide-block li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.85em; width: 5px; height: 5px; background: var(--border); }
  .guide-block strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  .guide-note { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }
</style>
